<headroom-library version="1" id="hg-sunset-strip-lead" category="High Gain" order="20" instrument="guitar" style="Hard Rock / Glam">
  <description>Glossy 80s arena-metal lead: a low-drive overdrive kicking a hot-rodded 100-watt Plexi with the bass down and presence up, into a 4x12, then a light chorus, a quarter-second-plus echo and a big hall. Bend, wail and let the repeats fill the gaps.</description>
  <tags><tag>High Gain</tag><tag>Hard Rock / Glam</tag><tag>80s</tag><tag>Lead</tag><tag>Chorus</tag><tag>Delay</tag><tag>Hall</tag></tags>
  <sources>
    <source url="http://www.woodytone.com/2010/01/04/warren-demartinis-1987-ratt-rig-part-1/" title="WoodyTone: Warren DeMartini's 1987 Ratt rig"/>
    <source url="https://www.guitarplayer.com/players/be-careful-what-you-wish-for-warren-demartini-tells-the-tale-of-ratts-1984-breakthrough-hit-round-and-round" title="Guitar Player: Warren DeMartini on Ratt's 1984 breakthrough"/>
    <source url="http://www.rebbeach.com/history_faq_gear.htm" title="Reb Beach: history and gear FAQ"/>
    <source url="https://gearspace.com/board/high-end/77436-george-lynch-tone.html" title="Gearspace: George Lynch tone thread (forum)"/>
  </sources>
</headroom-library>
